nested `(or …)` in a `:match` premise: SForm(head=Atom(name='or'), args=(SForm(head=Atom(name='p'), args=(Var(name='x'),)), SForm(head=Atom(name='q'), args=(Var(name='x'),)))). Only a TOP-LEVEL `(or …)` is supported (S1.8.A13 splits it into one plan per disjunct); a nested one needs DNF expansion, which the M1 compiler does not do. Lift the disjunction to the top of the `:match`, or split the rule.
